---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii2_34",
  "series": "Band II 2 (1686 - 1694)",
  "seq": 34,
  "text": "<p> [[148.1]] <b>35. LEIBNIZ FÜR JOHANN VAGETIUS</p>\n<p> [[148.2]] [Hannover, 20. Januar 1687.] [34.37.]</b></p>\n<p> [[148.14]] <b>Specimen Demonstratae consequentiae a rectis ad obliqua</b> </p>\n<p> [[148.15]] <k>Suppositio prima</i>, <b>sumta ex parte Logica de consequentia a rectis ad recta</b>:\n[[148.16]] Esse praedicatum in propositione universali affirmativa, idem est ac salva veritate loco subjecti\n[[148.17]] substitui posse in omni alia propositione affirmativa, ubi subjectum illud praedicati vice\n[[148.18]] fungitur. Et proinde ex praedicatione sequitur substitutio dicta, et contra ex substitutione\n[[148.19]] praedicatio. Exempli causa, <b>(pars prior)</b> quia <i>Graphice est ars</i>, si habeamus <i>rem quae est\n[[148.20]] Graphice</i>, substituere poterimus <i>rem quae est ars</i>. Et contra <b>(pars posterior)</b> si ostensum sit\n[[148.21]] pro eo <i>qui discit Graphicen</i> semper, salva veritate substitui dicto modo posse: <i>qui discit artem</i>,\n[[148.22]] vera erit propositio: <i>qui discit graphicen discit artem</i>. </p>\n<p> [[148.23]] <k>Suppositio secunda</i> <b>ex Grammatica casuum significatione</b>[:] Obliquo speciali\n[[148.24]] aequipollet obliquus generalis cum speciali recto. Et ideo sibi mutuo substitui possunt. Verbi\n[[149.1]] gratia, (<b>pars prior:)</b> pro termino: <i>qui discit graphicen</i>, substitui potest <i>qui discit rem quae est\n[[149.2]] graphice</i>. Et contra <b>(pars posterior:)</b> pro termino <i>qui discit rem quae est ars</i>, substitui\n[[149.3]] potest: <i>qui discit artem</i>. </p>\n<p> [[149.4]] <k>Suppositio tertia</i> Si ipsi <i>A</i> substitui potest <i>B</i>; et ipsi <i>B</i>, <i>C</i>, et ipsi <i>C</i>, <i>D</i>; etiam ipsi <i>A</i>\n[[149.5]] substitui potest <i>D</i>. </p>\n<p> [[149.6]] THEOREMA: A rectis ad obliqua valet consequentia. </p>\n<p> [[149.7]] Artic. (1) Esto in recto: <i>Graphice est ars</i>; </p>\n<p> [[149.8]] Artic. (2) ajo hinc sequi in obliquo: <i>qui discit Graphicen discit artem</i>.\n[[149.9]] Demonstratio </p>\n<p> [[149.10]] Artic. (3) Esto terminus: <i>qui discit graphicen</i>, </p>\n<p> [[149.11]] art. (4) pro eo substitui semper potest: <i>qui discit rem quae est graphice</i> (per partem\n[[149.12]] priorem suppositionis 2). </p>\n<p> [[149.13]] art. (5) pro quo rursus substitui semper supra dicto modo potest: <i>qui discit rem quae est\n[[149.14]] ars</i> (per partem priorem suppositionis 1. <i>Graphice</i> enim ex artic. 1, <i>est ars</i>). </p>\n<p> [[149.15]] Art. (6) At pro hoc iterum substitui semper potest: <i>qui discit artem</i> (per partem posteriorem\n[[149.16]] suppositionis 2). </p>\n<p> [[149.17]] art. (7) Ergo (per supp. 3) a primis ad ultima argumentando, (nempe ab articulo 3 per 4\n[[149.18]] et 5 ad 6) pro termino <i>qui discit graphicen</i> semper substitui supra dicto modo potest: <i>qui discit\n[[149.19]] artem</i>. </p>\n<p> [[149.20]] art. (8) Unde denique (per partem posteriorem supp. 1.) colligitur: <i>qui discit graphicen\n[[149.21]] discit artem</i> </p>\n<p> [[149.22]] Q.E.D. ut proponebatur artic. 2.\n[[149.23]] Scholium </p>\n<p> [[149.24]] Sciendum est ab obliquis ad recta vicissim non valere consequentiam. Neque enim\n[[149.25]] sequitur: <i>qui caedit os, caedit hominem, ergo os est homo</i>.\n[[150.1]] Brevius:\n[[150.2]] Supponitur\n [[150.3]] I. Consequentia a rectis ad recta\n [[150.4]] verbi gratia <i>Est graphice</i> ergo <i>est Ars</i>, quia <i>Gra</i><greek><i>f</i></greek><i>ice est ars</i>.\n [[150.5]] II. Aequipollentia obliqui specialis cum obliquo generali et recto speciali simul sumtis\n[[150.6]] v.g. inter <i>gra</i><greek><i>f</i></greek><i>icen</i> et <i>rem quae est graphice</i>.\n [[150.7]] III. Sorites. </p>\n<p> [[150.8]] Propositio: <i>Si Graphice est Ars qui discit Graphicen discit artem.</i>\n [[150.9]] Demonstratio </p>\n<p> [[150.10]] 1. Nam <i>qui discit Graphicen discit rem quae est Graphice</i> per suppos. 2. </p>\n<p> [[150.11]] 2. <i>Graphice</i> autem <i>est Ars</i>. </p>\n<p> [[150.12]] 3. Ergo <i>qui discit rem quae est Graphice discit rem quae est ars</i>\n [[150.13]] per artic. 2. juncta suppos. 1. </p>\n<p> [[150.14]] 4. Porro <i>qui discit rem quae est ars discit artem</i> per suppos. 2. </p>\n<p> [[150.15]] 5. Ergo <i>qui discit graphicen discit artem</i> per artic. 1, 2, 3[, 4] juncta suppos. 1. </p>\n",
  "number": "35.",
  "title": "LEIBNIZ FÜR JOHANN VAGETIUS",
  "date": "[Hannover, 20. Januar 1687.] [34.37.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:35. LEIBNIZ FÜR JOHANN VAGETIUS [Hannover, 20. Januar 1687.] [34.37.] Specimen Demonstratae consequentiae a rectis ad obliqua Suppositio prima, sumta ex parte Logica de consequentia a rectis ad recta: Esse praedicatum in propositione universali affirmativa, idem est ac salva veritate loco subjecti s...">
      <div class="text-content">
        {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
          paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
        )}
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>